{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-sci":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-sci/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prop-frobenius-positivity-filter","@type":["folio-assistant-sci:Proposition","doco:Section"],"label":"prop:frobenius-positivity-filter","kind":"proposition","title":"Frobenius positivity filter for even-$A$ decays","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-parity-regime-selection"],"tags":["frobenius","positivity","filter","even-A","config-exclusion"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.ParticleInteractions.frobenius_positivity_filter","text":"frobenius-positivity-filter.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"prop:frobenius-positivity-filter\"></a><p><em>For even <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code>: a channel configuration is Frobenius-positive if and only if both parent and daughter yield non-negative Markov traces.</em></p>\n<p><em>A configuration is excluded exactly when its sign-pattern has odd total parity. Of the <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">2^A</code> sign-patterns, exactly half are excluded.</em></p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/nuclear-interactions/frobenius-positivity-filter.md","heading":"Proposition","number":"14.10.8","page":"b/prop-frobenius-positivity-filter","qa":{"counts":{"pass":93,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":12,"unknown":0,"stale":79},"milnor":{"total":3,"notPassing":0}},"lean":{"expected":true,"ref":"qou:TwistedFrobeniusHopf.frobenius_positivity_filter","via":"ref","path":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/TwistedFrobeniusHopf/frobenius_positivity_filter.lean","compiles":"unchecked","sorry":false,"sorryBasis":"text"}}
